1
00:00:00,043 --> 00:00:01,044
GridBot Builder.

2
00:00:01,634 --> 00:00:02,784
GridBot Blueprint.

3
00:00:03,340 --> 00:00:04,074
Lesson one.

4
00:00:04,626 --> 00:00:05,355
Introduction.

5
00:00:06,470 --> 00:00:07,616
Education only.

6
00:00:08,175 --> 00:00:09,489
Not financial advice.

7
00:00:10,009 --> 00:00:12,061
This is general information and

8
00:00:12,061 --> 00:00:14,264
doesn't consider your objectives,

9
00:00:14,264 --> 00:00:16,164
financial situation or needs.

10
00:00:16,684 --> 00:00:18,883
Crypto, a digital coin, is high risk;

11
00:00:18,883 --> 00:00:21,319
you could lose all the money you put in.

12
00:00:21,839 --> 00:00:23,904
Past performance is not a reliable

13
00:00:23,904 --> 00:00:25,613
indicator of future results.

14
00:00:26,663 --> 00:00:29,056
The prices are public historical prices

15
00:00:29,056 --> 00:00:31,234
at the end of each day, marked Example.

16
00:00:32,367 --> 00:00:34,266
No order is sent from this lesson.

17
00:00:35,265 --> 00:00:37,164
By the end of this series you will

18
00:00:37,164 --> 00:00:38,952
understand what a grid bot does.

19
00:00:39,349 --> 00:00:40,801
It is a small program that

20
00:00:40,801 --> 00:00:42,366
places these orders for you.

21
00:00:42,822 --> 00:00:44,721
You will learn when it can capture

22
00:00:44,721 --> 00:00:46,285
bounces, and where it loses.

23
00:00:46,533 --> 00:00:48,544
You will know how to plan one, test

24
00:00:48,544 --> 00:00:50,443
it on paper, run it, check it, and

25
00:00:50,443 --> 00:00:52,491
change the capital you give to bots

26
00:00:52,491 --> 00:00:54,352
only under written risk rules.

27
00:00:54,872 --> 00:00:56,269
This is education, not

28
00:00:56,269 --> 00:00:57,589
a promise of results.

29
00:00:58,109 --> 00:00:59,719
Price often moves sideways,

30
00:00:59,719 --> 00:01:01,469
bouncing between the same top

31
00:01:01,469 --> 00:01:03,220
and bottom instead of leaving.

32
00:01:03,740 --> 00:01:05,450
A grid is a ladder of waiting

33
00:01:05,450 --> 00:01:07,159
orders, called limit orders,

34
00:01:07,159 --> 00:01:08,646
built for that bouncing.

35
00:01:09,166 --> 00:01:11,010
When price runs one way and stays

36
00:01:11,010 --> 00:01:13,188
there, the grid has nothing left to do.

37
00:01:13,569 --> 00:01:15,322
And if price falls through the

38
00:01:15,322 --> 00:01:17,005
bottom, coin means the crypto

39
00:01:17,005 --> 00:01:18,828
itself, and you are left holding

40
00:01:18,828 --> 00:01:20,560
the coin, and it is worth less.

41
00:01:21,491 --> 00:01:22,831
By the end you will know

42
00:01:22,831 --> 00:01:24,116
what a grid bot places.

43
00:01:25,246 --> 00:01:27,324
You will see that idea on

44
00:01:27,324 --> 00:01:29,299
one real path from 2023.

45
00:01:30,499 --> 00:01:32,008
You will be able to say the

46
00:01:32,008 --> 00:01:33,460
stop rule in one sentence.

47
00:01:34,414 --> 00:01:36,260
When a chart says Example, it

48
00:01:36,260 --> 00:01:38,106
means a real past price used

49
00:01:38,106 --> 00:01:39,952
as an example, not a forecast.

50
00:01:41,002 --> 00:01:42,243
Crypto is a digital

51
00:01:42,243 --> 00:01:43,641
asset, such as bitcoin.

52
00:01:44,161 --> 00:01:45,837
You do not need to have bought

53
00:01:45,837 --> 00:01:47,122
any before this lesson.

54
00:01:47,500 --> 00:01:49,467
An exchange is the website or app

55
00:01:49,467 --> 00:01:51,799
where you swap Australian dollars for

56
00:01:51,799 --> 00:01:53,840
crypto, and crypto back to dollars.

57
00:01:54,360 --> 00:01:56,036
This course does not name one,

58
00:01:56,036 --> 00:01:57,712
and it does not send an order.

59
00:01:58,457 --> 00:02:00,021
Cash is money you can spend.

60
00:02:00,423 --> 00:02:02,259
Here that means dollars, or a

61
00:02:02,259 --> 00:02:04,334
stablecoin, a crypto coin built

62
00:02:04,334 --> 00:02:05,850
to stay at one US dollar.

63
00:02:06,370 --> 00:02:08,437
We treat it like cash in this lesson,

64
00:02:08,437 --> 00:02:10,169
but it can drop below a dollar.

65
00:02:10,598 --> 00:02:12,789
Coin is the crypto, such as bitcoin.

66
00:02:13,839 --> 00:02:16,186
An order is an instruction to buy or sell.

67
00:02:16,638 --> 00:02:18,445
A buy order swaps cash for coin.

68
00:02:18,965 --> 00:02:20,868
A sell order swaps coin back to

69
00:02:20,868 --> 00:02:22,999
cash, and you can only sell coin you

70
00:02:22,999 --> 00:02:24,902
already hold, on a spot account.

71
00:02:25,422 --> 00:02:27,058
A spot account is the normal

72
00:02:27,058 --> 00:02:28,411
account on an exchange.

73
00:02:28,931 --> 00:02:30,327
You own the coin you buy,

74
00:02:30,327 --> 00:02:31,668
and nothing is borrowed.

75
00:02:32,550 --> 00:02:34,320
A bot is software that places

76
00:02:34,320 --> 00:02:35,942
and refills orders for you.

77
00:02:36,462 --> 00:02:38,305
You start with some cash and some

78
00:02:38,305 --> 00:02:39,981
coin, so there is something to

79
00:02:39,981 --> 00:02:41,713
buy with and something to sell.

80
00:02:41,762 --> 00:02:44,114
A grid bot places waiting buy orders

81
00:02:44,114 --> 00:02:46,466
on lines below the current price and

82
00:02:46,466 --> 00:02:48,819
sell orders on lines above it, inside

83
00:02:48,819 --> 00:02:50,622
a top and a bottom you choose.

84
00:02:51,142 --> 00:02:52,818
The space between your top and

85
00:02:52,818 --> 00:02:54,606
your bottom is called the range.

86
00:02:54,699 --> 00:02:56,805
The sells need some coin, so a grid

87
00:02:56,805 --> 00:02:58,754
starts with part cash and part

88
00:02:58,754 --> 00:03:00,704
coin, and that is a description,

89
00:03:00,704 --> 00:03:02,575
not advice about what to hold.

90
00:03:03,625 --> 00:03:05,331
A limit order is an order that

91
00:03:05,331 --> 00:03:06,895
waits at a price you choose.

92
00:03:07,415 --> 00:03:08,979
It does not chase the price.

93
00:03:09,399 --> 00:03:10,963
Chasing the price would mean

94
00:03:10,963 --> 00:03:12,415
moving the order to follow

95
00:03:12,415 --> 00:03:13,980
wherever the price has gone.

96
00:03:14,829 --> 00:03:16,904
An order fills when the price reaches

97
00:03:16,904 --> 00:03:18,636
its line and the trade happens.

98
00:03:19,097 --> 00:03:21,304
Until then, the order is only waiting.

99
00:03:22,354 --> 00:03:24,309
Think of a ladder leaned on a wall.

100
00:03:24,451 --> 00:03:26,797
The rungs wait, and they do not chase you.

101
00:03:27,073 --> 00:03:29,363
A rung is one price where an order waits.

102
00:03:29,770 --> 00:03:31,949
The gap is the space between two rungs.

103
00:03:32,238 --> 00:03:34,282
The ladder is the analogy, and the

104
00:03:34,282 --> 00:03:36,554
chart beside it is the real past path.

105
00:03:37,604 --> 00:03:39,015
The range is the top rung

106
00:03:39,015 --> 00:03:40,144
and the bottom rung.

107
00:03:40,664 --> 00:03:42,787
The levels are the rungs between them.

108
00:03:43,136 --> 00:03:45,427
The stop is the written rule for leaving.

109
00:03:46,276 --> 00:03:48,119
The range is the top line and the

110
00:03:48,119 --> 00:03:49,963
bottom line, taken from the path.

111
00:03:50,442 --> 00:03:51,930
Hindsight: this range is

112
00:03:51,930 --> 00:03:53,195
drawn after the fact.

113
00:03:53,715 --> 00:03:56,939
The chart is bitcoin's real daily

114
00:03:56,939 --> 00:04:00,509
closes from 19 July to 16 October 2023.

115
00:04:01,029 --> 00:04:02,481
Every close in this window

116
00:04:02,481 --> 00:04:04,213
stayed between those two lines.

117
00:04:04,999 --> 00:04:07,405
Six gaps of about 900 dollars each sit

118
00:04:07,405 --> 00:04:09,966
between the bottom line and the top line.

119
00:04:10,486 --> 00:04:12,713
Each gap is about 900 dollars:

120
00:04:12,713 --> 00:04:14,940
the top line minus the bottom

121
00:04:14,940 --> 00:04:16,424
line, divided by six.

122
00:04:16,944 --> 00:04:18,289
It is one step between

123
00:04:18,289 --> 00:04:19,858
lines, not the whole range.

124
00:04:20,378 --> 00:04:22,217
Seven lines make those six gaps.

125
00:04:22,737 --> 00:04:24,525
The levels are the prices on the

126
00:04:24,525 --> 00:04:26,201
rungs where limit orders wait.

127
00:04:27,187 --> 00:04:28,545
Buy orders wait on lines

128
00:04:28,545 --> 00:04:29,903
below the current price.

129
00:04:30,423 --> 00:04:32,379
Sell orders wait on lines above it.

130
00:04:32,860 --> 00:04:35,359
Each fill changes what you hold: a buy

131
00:04:35,359 --> 00:04:38,025
fill adds coin, and a sell fill adds cash.

132
00:04:38,545 --> 00:04:39,718
You choose the range,

133
00:04:39,718 --> 00:04:41,003
the gaps and the money.

134
00:04:41,312 --> 00:04:42,765
The bot places each order.

135
00:04:43,771 --> 00:04:45,621
After a fill, the bot places the

136
00:04:45,621 --> 00:04:47,694
opposite order one rung up or down.

137
00:04:48,214 --> 00:04:50,392
A buy fill gets a sell one rung higher.

138
00:04:50,779 --> 00:04:53,008
A sell fill gets a buy one rung lower.

139
00:04:53,528 --> 00:04:55,148
You still write the stop, and

140
00:04:55,148 --> 00:04:56,824
you act when that rule is met.

141
00:04:57,056 --> 00:04:59,291
The bot does not decide the stop for you

142
00:04:59,291 --> 00:05:01,414
unless you turned that setting on, and

143
00:05:01,414 --> 00:05:03,481
you write which one before you start.

144
00:05:04,215 --> 00:05:05,556
Think of a market stall.

145
00:05:05,988 --> 00:05:08,102
The stallholder buys stock a little

146
00:05:08,102 --> 00:05:10,216
cheaper and sells it a little dearer,

147
00:05:10,216 --> 00:05:11,836
and pays a fee on every sale.

148
00:05:12,286 --> 00:05:13,856
Exchanges charge a small

149
00:05:13,856 --> 00:05:14,902
fee on each trade.

150
00:05:15,422 --> 00:05:17,165
A grid can do that while price

151
00:05:17,165 --> 00:05:18,691
bounces inside the range.

152
00:05:19,211 --> 00:05:21,732
A bounce means price moves down and back

153
00:05:21,732 --> 00:05:24,101
up, or up and back down, and stays inside.

154
00:05:24,621 --> 00:05:26,857
One buy at a lower line and the later

155
00:05:26,857 --> 00:05:28,940
sell of that same coin is one pair.

156
00:05:29,460 --> 00:05:31,640
On these daily closes, the July to

157
00:05:31,640 --> 00:05:33,900
October example window finished

158
00:05:33,900 --> 00:05:36,000
only three pairs, each a buy and a

159
00:05:36,000 --> 00:05:38,099
sell on lines next to each other.

160
00:05:38,619 --> 00:05:40,351
The sell line is higher, so the

161
00:05:40,351 --> 00:05:42,195
cash that comes back is more than

162
00:05:42,195 --> 00:05:44,150
the cash that left, before the fee.

163
00:05:44,443 --> 00:05:45,896
A fee is what the exchange

164
00:05:45,896 --> 00:05:47,460
charges when an order fills.

165
00:05:47,641 --> 00:05:49,931
The fees come out of what the pair makes.

166
00:05:49,993 --> 00:05:51,501
If the fees are larger than

167
00:05:51,501 --> 00:05:53,121
that, the pair keeps nothing.

168
00:05:53,295 --> 00:05:54,538
This is not a promise.

169
00:05:55,058 --> 00:05:56,862
The pair finishes only if price

170
00:05:56,862 --> 00:05:58,735
does bounce and both orders fill.

171
00:05:59,785 --> 00:06:01,014
The daily close is the

172
00:06:01,014 --> 00:06:02,243
last price of the day.

173
00:06:02,664 --> 00:06:04,464
Crypto trades all day, so the

174
00:06:04,464 --> 00:06:05,872
day is cut at a set time.

175
00:06:06,392 --> 00:06:08,714
This lesson uses the end of each

176
00:06:08,714 --> 00:06:10,857
UTC day, the world's standard

177
00:06:10,857 --> 00:06:13,358
clock, which is 11am Sydney time in

178
00:06:13,358 --> 00:06:15,769
daylight saving, 10am otherwise.

179
00:06:16,289 --> 00:06:18,273
This is a simple candle that shows

180
00:06:18,273 --> 00:06:19,949
the day's high, low and close.

181
00:06:20,422 --> 00:06:22,352
Traders call it a candle because

182
00:06:22,352 --> 00:06:24,281
the full version has a thick body

183
00:06:24,281 --> 00:06:26,013
and a thin wick, like a candle.

184
00:06:26,445 --> 00:06:27,953
Here we only need the high,

185
00:06:27,953 --> 00:06:29,182
the low and the close.

186
00:06:29,516 --> 00:06:32,695
This candle is 19 July 2023.

187
00:06:33,215 --> 00:06:34,444
The high, the low, and

188
00:06:34,444 --> 00:06:35,729
the close are labelled.

189
00:06:36,622 --> 00:06:38,751
The example is Bitcoin's public

190
00:06:38,751 --> 00:06:40,407
daily price in US dollars.

191
00:06:40,927 --> 00:06:44,105
From 19 July 2023 to 16 October

192
00:06:44,105 --> 00:06:47,028
2023, every one of those days

193
00:06:47,028 --> 00:06:49,570
closed inside the range.

194
00:06:50,090 --> 00:06:51,763
The close crossed the seven

195
00:06:51,763 --> 00:06:53,509
lines 28 times in that window.

196
00:06:54,029 --> 00:06:56,341
The count is an example, not a forecast.

197
00:06:56,861 --> 00:06:58,649
We do not need to read each day.

198
00:06:58,915 --> 00:07:00,257
The shape is the lesson,

199
00:07:00,257 --> 00:07:01,671
and it is marked Example.

200
00:07:02,191 --> 00:07:04,947
Worked check: 19 July

201
00:07:04,947 --> 00:07:08,027
2023 to 16 October 2023.

202
00:07:08,547 --> 00:07:10,056
The low is the bottom line.

203
00:07:10,536 --> 00:07:12,002
The high is the top line.

204
00:07:12,522 --> 00:07:14,366
Nothing on this card is an order.

205
00:07:15,329 --> 00:07:18,172
Those 28 crossings, each time the price

206
00:07:18,172 --> 00:07:20,571
crosses a line, are not 28 results.

207
00:07:21,091 --> 00:07:23,293
A crossing only means the close moved

208
00:07:23,293 --> 00:07:25,360
from one side of a line to the other.

209
00:07:25,802 --> 00:07:27,513
A pair is finished only when a

210
00:07:27,513 --> 00:07:29,367
buy and its later sell have both

211
00:07:29,367 --> 00:07:31,099
filled, and only after the fee.

212
00:07:31,599 --> 00:07:33,498
The price can cross many lines and

213
00:07:33,498 --> 00:07:35,397
still leave you holding coin if it

214
00:07:35,397 --> 00:07:37,018
walks out through the bottom.

215
00:07:37,554 --> 00:07:39,062
You can buy part of a coin.

216
00:07:39,611 --> 00:07:42,571
Here we buy one hundredth

217
00:07:42,612 --> 00:07:43,673
of a bitcoin, 0.01.

218
00:07:43,673 --> 00:07:46,936
900 dollars times 0.01 bitcoin

219
00:07:46,936 --> 00:07:49,459
is 9 dollars before fees.

220
00:07:49,979 --> 00:07:52,960
In this example a buy waiting at the

221
00:07:52,960 --> 00:07:56,250
lower of these two lines was reached on

222
00:07:56,250 --> 00:07:59,231
17 August 2023, and the sell one line

223
00:07:59,231 --> 00:08:02,212
above was reached on 29 August 2023.

224
00:08:02,732 --> 00:08:04,520
The card shows the gap, then the

225
00:08:04,520 --> 00:08:06,084
two fees, then what is left.

226
00:08:06,393 --> 00:08:09,721
Each fee is 0.1 percent of the whole

227
00:08:09,721 --> 00:08:13,280
trade, not of the profit: about 27 cents

228
00:08:13,280 --> 00:08:16,608
on the 267 dollar buy and 28 cents on

229
00:08:16,608 --> 00:08:20,167
the 276 dollar sell, 54 cents together.

230
00:08:20,687 --> 00:08:22,511
That is about 8 dollars 46

231
00:08:22,511 --> 00:08:24,596
after fees, for one small pair.

232
00:08:25,116 --> 00:08:27,016
It happens only if the price comes

233
00:08:27,016 --> 00:08:28,692
back up through the sell line.

234
00:08:28,796 --> 00:08:30,528
If the price leaves through the

235
00:08:30,528 --> 00:08:32,315
bottom, you still hold the coin,

236
00:08:32,315 --> 00:08:33,880
and the pair never finishes.

237
00:08:34,072 --> 00:08:35,859
This card is not money you made.

238
00:08:36,257 --> 00:08:38,604
Past results don't predict future results.

239
00:08:45,592 --> 00:08:47,380
Now watch what you hold when the

240
00:08:47,380 --> 00:08:49,447
price leaves the range and stays out.

241
00:08:49,826 --> 00:08:51,502
Above the range the sells have

242
00:08:51,502 --> 00:08:53,290
filled and you are holding cash,

243
00:08:53,290 --> 00:08:54,742
with nothing left to sell.

244
00:08:55,064 --> 00:08:56,684
Below the range the buys have

245
00:08:56,684 --> 00:08:58,137
filled and you are holding

246
00:08:58,137 --> 00:08:59,869
coin, with nothing left to buy.

247
00:09:00,246 --> 00:09:01,638
That is why the way down

248
00:09:01,638 --> 00:09:03,397
matters most: every buy fills,

249
00:09:03,397 --> 00:09:05,155
and you are left holding coin.

250
00:09:07,205 --> 00:09:09,440
Here is that stop rule on the real path.

251
00:09:09,860 --> 00:09:12,205
It triggers if a daily close is outside

252
00:09:12,205 --> 00:09:14,550
the range, through the top or the bottom,

253
00:09:14,550 --> 00:09:17,042
and the next daily close is still outside.

254
00:09:17,562 --> 00:09:19,014
Then the idea is finished.

255
00:09:19,394 --> 00:09:21,488
You stop the bot, which cancels the

256
00:09:21,488 --> 00:09:23,357
waiting orders, and do what you

257
00:09:23,357 --> 00:09:25,451
wrote: keep the coin or swap to cash.

258
00:09:25,971 --> 00:09:27,953
A bot's automatic stop is a price

259
00:09:27,953 --> 00:09:29,641
that can fire during the day.

260
00:09:30,161 --> 00:09:31,860
This course uses the two daily

261
00:09:31,860 --> 00:09:33,696
closes, unless your written plan

262
00:09:33,696 --> 00:09:35,484
says you turned on a price stop.

263
00:09:35,916 --> 00:09:37,256
This is a teaching rule,

264
00:09:37,256 --> 00:09:38,434
not a recommendation.

265
00:09:38,954 --> 00:09:40,574
The stop is your written rule

266
00:09:40,574 --> 00:09:42,027
for when you stop the bot.

267
00:09:42,259 --> 00:09:44,393
On 23 October 2023 the close

268
00:09:44,393 --> 00:09:46,805
finished above the top line, and

269
00:09:46,805 --> 00:09:49,124
the next day was still above it.

270
00:09:54,174 --> 00:09:55,627
Through the top, the sells

271
00:09:55,627 --> 00:09:57,303
have filled and you hold cash.

272
00:09:57,412 --> 00:09:59,255
Through the bottom, the buys have

273
00:09:59,255 --> 00:10:01,099
filled and you hold coin that you

274
00:10:01,099 --> 00:10:03,110
bought above where the price is now.

275
00:10:03,469 --> 00:10:04,922
That loss can keep growing

276
00:10:04,922 --> 00:10:06,039
until the stop acts.

277
00:10:06,344 --> 00:10:08,188
You stop the bot either way, then

278
